# Binary files — prevent Git from applying autocrlf line-ending
# normalisation on Windows checkouts. The Phase-1 commit of the land
# mask shipped 810001 bytes instead of 810000 because this file was
# missing; bytes 0x0a were silently rewritten to 0x0d0a on check-in.
*.bin binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.tar binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary

# Vendored geodata. Not binary in the "do not diff it" sense — it is text —
# but it must reach disk BYTE for byte, because the country outlines are
# NDJSON: `services/geo/countryBoundaries.ts` walks the file line by line and
# parses each one as a feature, so an appended \r sits after the closing brace
# and JSON.parse throws "Unexpected non-whitespace character after JSON".
#
# Measured 2026-09-03 on a Windows checkout: countries-10m.geojson came out
# 10195682 bytes against a 10195429-byte blob — 253 rewritten line endings,
# one per feature — and every caller of countryFromCoordinates() failed. That
# includes the Dawarich country-day sweep and the boundary check in the data
# quality inbox. marnet.geojson escaped with one byte and kept working only
# because its loader parses the whole file at once, where CR is whitespace.
#
# The Dockerfile COPYs both straight out of the build context, and this
# project builds its images locally — so on a Windows build host the corrupt
# file shipped into the image. Same failure the land mask had, same fix, one
# extension later.
*.geojson binary

# Machine-generated catalogues are written with LF by their generator
# (scripts/generate-airline-catalog.ts) and byte-compared against fresh
# generator output by the drift-guard test
# (backend/src/__tests__/dataIntegrity.airlineCatalog.test.ts). With
# core.autocrlf=true these files check out as CRLF on Windows, so the
# byte compare (LF generator vs CRLF on disk) failed. Pin LF so the guard
# is platform-stable.
frontend/src/lib/generated/*.ts text eol=lf
